    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0437" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.419/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-03T14:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                                1923—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:22 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>485. Following from Ambassador Harvey at Southampton.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“… Curzon was not available at the time I left London but I signed a
                            letter<anchor n="15a" xml:id="d208-f1"/> setting forth your proposals
                        respecting Newcastle consulate, which was delivered to the Foreign Office. …
                        Unless they change their minds the result in the case will be satisfactory
                        to you. Harvey.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
